  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"In the book we cycle through different perspectives of Critter's F, L, O, and P paintings, beginning with narrow views and ending with a more complete picture. Two paintings are compatible performative contradictions, and the other two are geometric post-impressionist-ish landscapes. With a multitude of possible readings, one can reasonably both agree and disagree with the arguments raised. Like lots of things, it's not one or the other that's true, but one and the other" -- Artist's statement from website, viewed 4 August 2023.</subfield>
